      "content": "Henderson (1984a) gives other equivalent conditions. Equation A3.6c implies that if $ \\mathbf{X}^T\\mathbf{X} $ is nonsingular, all linear combinations of $ \\beta $ are estimable. Note that Equation A3.6c is identical to the condition given by Equation A3.5a (taking $ \\mathbf{A} = \\mathbf{X}^T\\mathbf{X} $), implying that these solutions are also unique estimates. If estimable, the OLS solution of the vector $ \\mathbf{b}^T\\beta $ given by",
